 #define GUNCON_CAL_TOLERANCE 13107
 
+/* Half-window around the centre, as a percentage of the calibrated span of
+ * each axis, for the "shoot here to start" bullseye of the test phase. The
+ * drawn bullseye is only ~2.5% of that span; we accept anything in the
+ * middle ~30% of the screen, deliberately generous. Test shots meant to
+ * check the aim land on the edges anyway.
+ *
+ * It has to be expressed against the calibration bbox, not in absolute units:
+ * the captured lock is the RAW gun position (lightgun_filter_screen_axis
+ * records last_screen_* before applying the cal remap), so screen centre is
+ * the middle of [cal_min, cal_max], not 0. The three targets are symmetric
+ * about the screen centre, so that midpoint is exactly it.
+ *
+ * Validating by shooting is the only reliable option: on the gun's port the
+ * joypad-only binds (START, SELECT, D-pad) are unreadable. */
+#define GUNCON_CAL_CENTER_PCT 15
+
